  "content": {
    "id": "v2-c-p54-applications-slot-10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "A netball is shot towards the goal. Its path is a parabola with its highest point 6 metres above the ground, 4 metres horizontally from the shooter. The ball leaves the shooter's hands 2 metres above the ground.\n\nLet $x$ be the horizontal distance from the shooter and $y$ the height, both in metres. Write an equation in the form $y=ax^2+bx+c$ to model the ball's path.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$y=-\\dfrac14x^2+2x+2$",
      "worked": "The vertex is $(4,6)$.\n$$y=a(x-4)^2+6$$\nThe ball starts at $(0,2)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2&=a(0-4)^2+6\\\\2&=16a+6\\\\a&=-\\frac14\\\\y&=-\\frac14(x-4)^2+6\\\\y&=-\\frac14(x^2-8x+16)+6\\\\y&=-\\frac14x^2+2x+2\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": null
  },
